Space‑based Laser Communication refers to optical systems that employ highly directional laser beams to transmit high‑speed data between satellites, space stations, deep‑space probes and ground stations. Unlike conventional radio‑frequency links, these terminals-comprising laser transmitters, optical receivers, precision pointing mechanisms, telescopes and radiation‑hard electronics-deliver markedly higher bandwidth, lower latency and enhanced security while alleviating spectrum congestion.
