What is Space‑based Laser Communication?
Space‑based Laser Communication (also known as optical inter‑satellite links) is a technology that uses coherent or direct‑detection laser beams to convey data across the vacuum of space. The core advantages over radio‑frequency (RF) systems include:
Higher data rates-often measured in multiple gigabits per second-thanks to the short wavelength of light.
Reduced payload mass and power consumption because optical terminals can be smaller and more efficient.
Intrinsic security, as narrow laser beams are difficult to intercept or jam.
Freedom from crowded RF spectrum, which is increasingly regulated and congested.
